    /// @answers whether the receiver is less than `other`, a Boolean:
    /// false whenever either side is a NaN.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `other`, '< requires a numeric
    /// argument, got …', for any other argument.
    public < other = (
      ^vmMirror float: self lessThan: other ifFail: [^super < other].
    )

    /// As `<`, whether the receiver is greater.
    ///
    /// @param other a number.
    /// @answers whether the receiver is greater than `other`, a Boolean:
    /// false whenever either side is a NaN.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `other`, '> requires a numeric
    /// argument, got …', for any other argument.
    /// @see `<`.
    public > other = (
      ^vmMirror float: self greaterThan: other ifFail: [^super > other].
    )

    /// As `<`, whether the receiver is less or equal.
    ///
    /// @param other a number.
    /// @answers whether the receiver is less than or equal to `other`, a
    /// Boolean: false whenever either side is a NaN.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `other`, '<= requires a numeric
    /// argument, got …', for any other argument.
    /// @see `<`.
    public <= other = (
      ^vmMirror float: self lessOrEqual: other ifFail: [^super <= other].
    )

    /// As `<`, whether the receiver is greater or equal.
    ///
    /// @param other a number.
    /// @answers whether the receiver is greater than or equal to `other`,
    /// a Boolean: false whenever either side is a NaN.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `other`, '>= requires a numeric
    /// argument, got …', for any other argument.
    /// @see `<`.
    public >= other = (
      ^vmMirror float: self greaterOrEqual: other ifFail: [^super >= other].
    )

