    /// @answers the Integer from -2147483648 to 2147483647 there.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `position`, 'int32At: position … out of
    /// range: valid positions are 1..… (size …)' or, when `bytes` holds fewer
    /// than 4 bytes, 'int32At: position … out of range: no position holds 4
    /// bytes (size …)', for an Integer outside 1 to `size` - 3, a LargeInteger
    /// included.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `position`, 'int32At: requires an
    /// Integer position, got …', for a position that is no Integer.
    /// @signals ArgumentError of `noByteArray:` when `bytes` holds no
    /// ByteArray.
    /// @see `noByteArray:`.
    public int32At: position = (
      ^vmMirror byteArray: bytes bigEndianInt32At: position ifFail: [^self noByteArray: #int32At:].
    )

    /// Stores `value` at byte position `position`, big-endian, in the 4 bytes
    /// from `position` on. A refused store leaves the bytes as they were.
    ///
    /// @param position an Integer from 1 to `size` - 3.
    /// @param value an Integer from -2147483648 to 2147483647.
    /// @answers `value` itself.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `position`, 'int32At:put: position … out
    /// of range: valid positions are 1..… (size …)' or, when `bytes` holds
    /// fewer than 4 bytes, 'int32At:put: position … out of range: no position
    /// holds 4 bytes (size …)', for an Integer outside 1 to `size` - 3, a
    /// LargeInteger included.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `position`, 'int32At:put: requires an
    /// Integer position, got …', for a position that is no Integer.
    /// @signals ArgumentError of `noByteArray:` when `bytes` holds no
    /// ByteArray.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `value`, 'int32At:put: requires an
    /// Integer from -2147483648 to 2147483647, got …', for a value outside that
    /// range or no Integer, at a valid position.
    /// @see `noByteArray:`.
    public int32At: position put: value = (
      ^vmMirror byteArray: bytes bigEndianInt32At: position put: value ifFail: [
        ^self noByteArray: #int32At:put:.
      ].
    )

    /// Reads the unsigned 32-bit Integer at byte position `position`,
    /// big-endian, in the 4 bytes from `position` on.
    ///
    /// @param position an Integer from 1 to `size` - 3.
    /// @answers the Integer from 0 to 4294967295 there.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `position`, 'uint32At: position … out of
    /// range: valid positions are 1..… (size …)' or, when `bytes` holds fewer
    /// than 4 bytes, 'uint32At: position … out of range: no position holds 4
    /// bytes (size …)', for an Integer outside 1 to `size` - 3, a LargeInteger
    /// included.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `position`, 'uint32At: requires an
    /// Integer position, got …', for a position that is no Integer.
    /// @signals ArgumentError of `noByteArray:` when `bytes` holds no
    /// ByteArray.
    /// @see `noByteArray:`.
    public uint32At: position = (
      ^vmMirror byteArray: bytes bigEndianUint32At: position ifFail: [
        ^self noByteArray: #uint32At:.
      ].
    )

    /// Stores `value` at byte position `position`, big-endian, in the 4 bytes
    /// from `position` on. A refused store leaves the bytes as they were.
    ///
    /// @param position an Integer from 1 to `size` - 3.
    /// @param value an Integer from 0 to 4294967295.
    /// @answers `value` itself.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `position`, 'uint32At:put: position …
    /// out of range: valid positions are 1..… (size …)' or, when `bytes` holds
    /// fewer than 4 bytes, 'uint32At:put: position … out of range: no position
    /// holds 4 bytes (size …)', for an Integer outside 1 to `size` - 3, a
    /// LargeInteger included.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `position`, 'uint32At:put: requires an
    /// Integer position, got …', for a position that is no Integer.
    /// @signals ArgumentError of `noByteArray:` when `bytes` holds no
    /// ByteArray.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `value`, 'uint32At:put: requires an
    /// Integer from 0 to 4294967295, got …', for a value outside that range or
    /// no Integer, at a valid position.
    /// @see `noByteArray:`.
    public uint32At: position put: value = (
      ^vmMirror byteArray: bytes bigEndianUint32At: position put: value ifFail: [
        ^self noByteArray: #uint32At:put:.
      ].
    )

    /// Reads the signed 64-bit Integer at byte position `position`, big-endian,
    /// in the 8 bytes from `position` on.
    ///
    /// @param position an Integer from 1 to `size` - 7.
    /// @answers the Integer from -9223372036854775808 to 9223372036854775807
    /// there.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `position`, 'int64At: position … out of
    /// range: valid positions are 1..… (size …)' or, when `bytes` holds fewer
    /// than 8 bytes, 'int64At: position … out of range: no position holds 8
    /// bytes (size …)', for an Integer outside 1 to `size` - 7, a LargeInteger
    /// included.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `position`, 'int64At: requires an
    /// Integer position, got …', for a position that is no Integer.
    /// @signals ArgumentError of `noByteArray:` when `bytes` holds no
    /// ByteArray.
    /// @see `noByteArray:`.
    public int64At: position = (
      ^vmMirror byteArray: bytes bigEndianInt64At: position ifFail: [^self noByteArray: #int64At:].
    )

    /// Stores `value` at byte position `position`, big-endian, in the 8 bytes
    /// from `position` on. A refused store leaves the bytes as they were.
    ///
    /// @param position an Integer from 1 to `size` - 7.
    /// @param value an Integer from -9223372036854775808 to
    /// 9223372036854775807.
    /// @answers `value` itself.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `position`, 'int64At:put: position … out
    /// of range: valid positions are 1..… (size …)' or, when `bytes` holds
    /// fewer than 8 bytes, 'int64At:put: position … out of range: no position
    /// holds 8 bytes (size …)', for an Integer outside 1 to `size` - 7, a
    /// LargeInteger included.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `position`, 'int64At:put: requires an
    /// Integer position, got …', for a position that is no Integer.
    /// @signals ArgumentError of `noByteArray:` when `bytes` holds no
    /// ByteArray.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `value`, 'int64At:put: requires an
    /// Integer from -9223372036854775808 to 9223372036854775807, got …', for a
    /// value outside that range or no Integer, at a valid position.
    /// @see `noByteArray:`.
    public int64At: position put: value = (
      ^vmMirror byteArray: bytes bigEndianInt64At: position put: value ifFail: [
        ^self noByteArray: #int64At:put:.
      ].
    )

    /// Reads the unsigned 64-bit Integer at byte position `position`,
    /// big-endian, in the 8 bytes from `position` on.
    ///
    /// @param position an Integer from 1 to `size` - 7.
    /// @answers the Integer from 0 to 18446744073709551615 there.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `position`, 'uint64At: position … out of
    /// range: valid positions are 1..… (size …)' or, when `bytes` holds fewer
    /// than 8 bytes, 'uint64At: position … out of range: no position holds 8
    /// bytes (size …)', for an Integer outside 1 to `size` - 7, a LargeInteger
    /// included.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `position`, 'uint64At: requires an
    /// Integer position, got …', for a position that is no Integer.
    /// @signals ArgumentError of `noByteArray:` when `bytes` holds no
    /// ByteArray.
    /// @see `noByteArray:`.
    public uint64At: position = (
      ^vmMirror byteArray: bytes bigEndianUint64At: position ifFail: [
        ^self noByteArray: #uint64At:.
      ].
    )

    /// Stores `value` at byte position `position`, big-endian, in the 8 bytes
    /// from `position` on. A refused store leaves the bytes as they were.
    ///
    /// @param position an Integer from 1 to `size` - 7.
    /// @param value an Integer from 0 to 18446744073709551615.
    /// @answers `value` itself.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `position`, 'uint64At:put: position …
    /// out of range: valid positions are 1..… (size …)' or, when `bytes` holds
    /// fewer than 8 bytes, 'uint64At:put: position … out of range: no position
    /// holds 8 bytes (size …)', for an Integer outside 1 to `size` - 7, a
    /// LargeInteger included.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `position`, 'uint64At:put: requires an
    /// Integer position, got …', for a position that is no Integer.
    /// @signals ArgumentError of `noByteArray:` when `bytes` holds no
    /// ByteArray.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `value`, 'uint64At:put: requires an
    /// Integer from 0 to 18446744073709551615, got …', for a value outside that
    /// range or no Integer, at a valid position.
    /// @see `noByteArray:`.
    public uint64At: position put: value = (
      ^vmMirror byteArray: bytes bigEndianUint64At: position put: value ifFail: [
        ^self noByteArray: #uint64At:put:.
      ].
    )

    /// Reads the binary32 at byte position `position`, big-endian, in the 4
    /// bytes from `position` on, and widens it exactly.
    ///
    /// @param position an Integer from 1 to `size` - 3.
    /// @answers the Float there.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `position`, 'float32At: position … out
    /// of range: valid positions are 1..… (size …)' or, when `bytes` holds
    /// fewer than 4 bytes, 'float32At: position … out of range: no position
    /// holds 4 bytes (size …)', for an Integer outside 1 to `size` - 3, a
    /// LargeInteger included.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `position`, 'float32At: requires an
    /// Integer position, got …', for a position that is no Integer.
    /// @signals ArgumentError of `noByteArray:` when `bytes` holds no
    /// ByteArray.
    /// @see `noByteArray:`.
    public float32At: position = (
      ^vmMirror byteArray: bytes bigEndianFloat32At: position ifFail: [
        ^self noByteArray: #float32At:.
      ].
    )

    /// Stores `value` at byte position `position`, big-endian, converted as
    /// `asFloat` converts it and rounded to binary32, in the 4 bytes from
    /// `position` on. A refused store leaves the bytes as they were.
    ///
    /// The leaf takes only a Float, so the conversion happens here; a value
    /// that is no Number reaches the leaf as it is, so that the position is
    /// checked first and the refusal names the value given.
    ///
    /// @param position an Integer from 1 to `size` - 3.
    /// @param value a Number.
    /// @answers `value` itself.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `position`, 'float32At:put: position …
    /// out of range: valid positions are 1..… (size …)' or, when `bytes` holds
    /// fewer than 4 bytes, 'float32At:put: position … out of range: no position
    /// holds 4 bytes (size …)', for an Integer outside 1 to `size` - 3, a
    /// LargeInteger included.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `position`, 'float32At:put: requires an
    /// Integer position, got …', for a position that is no Integer.
    /// @signals ArgumentError of `noByteArray:` when `bytes` holds no
    /// ByteArray.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `value`, 'float32At:put: requires a
    /// Number, got …', for a value that is no Number, at a valid position.
    /// @see `noByteArray:`.
    public float32At: position put: value = (
      vmMirror byteArray: bytes
          bigEndianFloat32At: position
          put: (value isKindOfNumber ifTrue: [value asFloat] ifFalse: [value])
          ifFail: [^self noByteArray: #float32At:put:].
      ^value.
    )

    /// Reads the binary64 at byte position `position`, big-endian, in the 8
    /// bytes from `position` on.
    ///
    /// @param position an Integer from 1 to `size` - 7.
    /// @answers the Float there.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `position`, 'float64At: position … out
    /// of range: valid positions are 1..… (size …)' or, when `bytes` holds
    /// fewer than 8 bytes, 'float64At: position … out of range: no position
    /// holds 8 bytes (size …)', for an Integer outside 1 to `size` - 7, a
    /// LargeInteger included.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `position`, 'float64At: requires an
    /// Integer position, got …', for a position that is no Integer.
    /// @signals ArgumentError of `noByteArray:` when `bytes` holds no
    /// ByteArray.
    /// @see `noByteArray:`.
    public float64At: position = (
      ^vmMirror byteArray: bytes bigEndianFloat64At: position ifFail: [
        ^self noByteArray: #float64At:.
      ].
    )

    /// Stores `value` at byte position `position`, big-endian, converted as
    /// `asFloat` converts it, in the 8 bytes from `position` on. A refused
    /// store leaves the bytes as they were.
    ///
    /// The leaf takes only a Float, so the conversion happens here; a value
    /// that is no Number reaches the leaf as it is, so that the position is
    /// checked first and the refusal names the value given.
    ///
    /// @param position an Integer from 1 to `size` - 7.
    /// @param value a Number.
    /// @answers `value` itself.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `position`, 'float64At:put: position …
    /// out of range: valid positions are 1..… (size …)' or, when `bytes` holds
    /// fewer than 8 bytes, 'float64At:put: position … out of range: no position
    /// holds 8 bytes (size …)', for an Integer outside 1 to `size` - 7, a
    /// LargeInteger included.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `position`, 'float64At:put: requires an
    /// Integer position, got …', for a position that is no Integer.
    /// @signals ArgumentError of `noByteArray:` when `bytes` holds no
    /// ByteArray.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying `value`, 'float64At:put: requires a
    /// Number, got …', for a value that is no Number, at a valid position.
    /// @see `noByteArray:`.
    public float64At: position put: value = (
      vmMirror byteArray: bytes
          bigEndianFloat64At: position
          put: (value isKindOfNumber ifTrue: [value asFloat] ifFalse: [value])
          ifFail: [^self noByteArray: #float64At:put:].
      ^value.
    )
  )

  /// The class of `nil`.
  ///
  /// §5.1.3: `nil` is the unique instance of `UndefinedObject`, which
  /// answers `isNil` with true. It answers the rest of the nil protocol
  /// `Object` declares the other way round, each a quick method, and
  /// prints as `nil`.
  public class UndefinedObject = Value () (
    /// Tells whether the receiver is nil, which it is.
    ///
    /// @answers true: the receiver is nil.
    public isNil = (
      ^true.
    )

    /// Tells whether the receiver is anything but nil, which it is not.
    ///
    /// @answers false: the receiver is nil.
    public notNil = (
      ^false.
    )

    /// Evaluates `block`, since the receiver is nil.
    ///
    /// @param block a block of no argument, or anything understanding
    /// `value`; sent `value`.
    /// @answers the value of `block`.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying the block, 'wrong number of block
    /// arguments: block takes …, got 0', for a block that declares
    /// parameters.
    public ifNil: block = (
      ^block value.
    )

    /// Leaves `block` alone: the receiver is nil, so `block` is not
    /// evaluated.
    ///
    /// @param block any object.
    /// @answers nil.
    public ifNotNil: block = (
      ^nil.
    )

    /// Evaluates `nilBlock`, since the receiver is nil; `notNilBlock` is
    /// not evaluated.
    ///
    /// @param nilBlock a block of no argument, or anything understanding
    /// `value`; sent `value`.
    /// @param notNilBlock any object.
    /// @answers the value of `nilBlock`.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying the block, 'wrong number of block
    /// arguments: block takes …, got 0', for a `nilBlock` that declares
    /// parameters.
    public ifNil: nilBlock ifNotNil: notNilBlock = (
      ^nilBlock value.
    )

    /// As `ifNil:ifNotNil:`, its arguments in the other order.
    ///
    /// @param notNilBlock any object; not evaluated.
    /// @param nilBlock as `ifNil:ifNotNil:`'s, sent `value`.
    /// @answers the value of `nilBlock`.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying the block, 'wrong number of block
    /// arguments: block takes …, got 0', for a `nilBlock` that declares
    /// parameters.
    /// @see `ifNil:ifNotNil:`.
    public ifNotNil: notNilBlock ifNil: nilBlock = (
      ^nilBlock value.
    )

    /// Describes the receiver as the literal that names it.
    ///
    /// @answers the String 'nil'.
    public printString = (
      ^'nil'.
    )
  )

  /// A closure, `[:argument | …]`: code that runs when it is sent
  /// `value`, in the scope it was written in (§5.1.8).
  ///
  /// A receiver holding no closure -- `Closure new`, an instance of a
  /// program's subclass of `Closure` -- makes every leaf decline: `value`,
  /// `value:`, `value:value:`, `value:value:value:` and `numArgs` end in
  /// `doesNotUnderstand:`, a MessageNotUnderstood, as does every member here
  /// whose sends reach them. The answers and Errors each member below names
  /// are those of a closure.
  public class Closure = Object () (
    /// Identifies the receiver as a Closure, without a class test.
    ///
    /// @answers true.
    public isKindOfClosure = (
      ^true.
    )

    /// Evaluates the block with no argument.
    ///
    /// @answers the block's value.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying the block, 'wrong number of block
    /// arguments: block takes …, got 0', when it declares any parameter.
    public value = (
      ^vmMirror blockValue: self ifFail: [^super value].
    )

    /// As `value`, with `first` as the block's one argument.
    ///
    /// @param first any object; the block's argument.
    /// @answers the block's value.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying the block, 'wrong number of block
    /// arguments: block takes …, got 1', when it does not declare exactly
    /// one parameter.
    /// @see `value`.
    public value: first = (
      ^vmMirror block: self value: first ifFail: [^super value: first].
    )

    /// As `value`, with two arguments, in order.
    ///
    /// @param first any object; the block's first argument.
    /// @param second any object; the block's second argument.
    /// @answers the block's value.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying the block, 'wrong number of block
    /// arguments: block takes …, got 2', when it does not declare exactly
    /// two parameters.
    /// @see `value`.
    public value: first value: second = (
      ^vmMirror block: self value: first value: second ifFail: [^super value: first value: second].
    )

    /// As `value`, with three arguments, in order.
    ///
    /// @param first any object; the block's first argument.
    /// @param second any object; the block's second argument.
    /// @param third any object; the block's third argument.
    /// @answers the block's value.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying the block, 'wrong number of block
    /// arguments: block takes …, got 3', when it does not declare exactly
    /// three parameters.
    /// @see `value`.
    public value: first value: second value: third = (
      ^vmMirror block: self value: first value: second value: third ifFail: [
        ^super value: first value: second value: third.
      ].
    )

    /// As `value`, with the elements of `arguments` as the block's
    /// arguments, in order, however many the block declares.
    ///
    /// The block is given the elements `arguments` holds when it is sent;
    /// a change the block makes to `arguments` changes none of its
    /// parameters. A collection that is no Array is copied into one first,
    /// in its `do:` order.
    ///
    /// @param arguments an Array, or a Collection or anything `Array
    /// withAll:` takes; its elements are the block's arguments.
    /// @answers the block's value.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying the block, 'wrong number of block
    /// arguments: block takes …, got …', when `arguments` does not hold
    /// exactly as many elements as the block declares parameters.
    /// @see `value`.
    public valueWithArguments: arguments = (
      ^vmMirror block: self valueWithArguments: arguments ifFail: [
        arguments isKindOfArray ifTrue: [^super valueWithArguments: arguments].
        ^self valueWithArguments: (Array withAll: arguments).
      ].
    )

    /// Counts the parameters the block declares, fixed when it was
    /// written.
    ///
    /// @answers the number of parameters the block declares, an Integer of
    /// at least 0.
    public numArgs = (
      ^vmMirror blockNumArgs: self ifFail: [^super numArgs].
    )

    /// Evaluates the block with `argument` when it declares parameters,
    /// and with none when it declares none.
    ///
    /// `Object`'s `ifNotNil:` family means exactly this, and its quick
    /// methods do it without sending it.
    ///
    /// @param argument any object.
    /// @answers the block's value.
    /// @signals ArgumentError of `value:`, carrying the block, 'wrong number
    /// of block arguments: block takes …, got 1', for a block of two
    /// parameters or more.
    /// @see `value:`.
    public cull: argument = (
      ^self numArgs = 0 ifTrue: [self value] ifFalse: [self value: argument].
    )

    /// Evaluates the block with as many of `first` and `second`, in that
    /// order, as it declares parameters: none, `first`, or both.
    ///
    /// @param first any object; the block's first argument.
    /// @param second any object; the block's second argument.
    /// @answers the block's value.
    /// @signals ArgumentError of `value:value:`, carrying the block, 'wrong
    /// number of block arguments: block takes …, got 2', for a block of
    /// three parameters or more.
    /// @see `cull:`.
    public cull: first cull: second = (
      |
        count = self numArgs.
      |
      count = 0 ifTrue: [^self value].
      count = 1 ifTrue: [^self value: first].
      ^self value: first value: second.
    )

    /// Evaluates the block with as many of `first`, `second` and `third`,
    /// in that order, as it declares parameters: none, one, two or all
    /// three.
    ///
    /// @param first any object; the block's first argument.
    /// @param second any object; the block's second argument.
    /// @param third any object; the block's third argument.
    /// @answers the block's value.
    /// @signals ArgumentError of `value:value:value:`, carrying the block,
    /// 'wrong number of block arguments: block takes …, got 3', for a block
    /// of four parameters or more.
    /// @see `cull:`.
    public cull: first cull: second cull: third = (
      |
        count = self numArgs.
      |
      count = 0 ifTrue: [^self value].
      count = 1 ifTrue: [^self value: first].
      count = 2 ifTrue: [^self value: first value: second].
      ^self value: first value: second value: third.
    )

    /// Evaluates the receiver and, while it answers true, `body`, then
    /// the receiver again, until it answers false.
    ///
    /// The compiler inlines a send of this message whose receiver and
    /// argument are block literals; this method serves every other
    /// send, and its own loop is that inlined form, whose guard signals
    /// the NonBooleanReceiver.
    ///
    /// @param body a block of no argument, or anything understanding
    /// `value`; sent `value`.
    /// @answers nil, once the receiver answers false.
    /// @signals NonBooleanReceiver carrying the answer, 'a loop's condition
    /// answered …, which is no Boolean', when the receiver answers anything
    /// but a Boolean.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying the block, 'wrong number of block
    /// arguments: block takes …, got 0', for a receiver that declares
    /// parameters, or a `body` that does, once the receiver answers true.
    public whileTrue: body = (
      ^[self value] whileTrue: [body value].
    )

    /// As `whileTrue:`, evaluating `body` while the receiver answers
    /// false.
    ///
    /// @param body a block of no argument, or anything understanding
    /// `value`; sent `value`.
    /// @answers nil, once the receiver answers true.
    /// @signals NonBooleanReceiver carrying the answer, 'a loop's condition
    /// answered …, which is no Boolean', when the receiver answers anything
    /// but a Boolean.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying the block, 'wrong number of block
    /// arguments: block takes …, got 0', for a receiver that declares
    /// parameters, or a `body` that does, once the receiver answers false.
    /// @see `whileTrue:`.
    public whileFalse: body = (
      ^[self value] whileFalse: [body value].
    )

    /// Evaluates the receiver again and again while it answers true.
    ///
    /// The compiler inlines a send of this message whose receiver is a
    /// block literal; this method serves every other send, and its own
    /// loop is that inlined form.
    ///
    /// @answers nil, once the receiver answers false.
    /// @signals NonBooleanReceiver carrying the answer, 'a loop's condition
    /// answered …, which is no Boolean', when the receiver answers anything
    /// but a Boolean.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying the block, 'wrong number of block
    /// arguments: block takes …, got 0', for a receiver that declares
    /// parameters.
    /// @see `whileTrue:`.
    public whileTrue = (
      ^[self value] whileTrue.
    )

    /// Evaluates the receiver again and again while it answers false.
    ///
    /// The compiler inlines a send of this message whose receiver is a
    /// block literal; this method serves every other send, and its own
    /// loop is that inlined form.
    ///
    /// @answers nil, once the receiver answers true.
    /// @signals NonBooleanReceiver carrying the answer, 'a loop's condition
    /// answered …, which is no Boolean', when the receiver answers anything
    /// but a Boolean.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying the block, 'wrong number of block
    /// arguments: block takes …, got 0', for a receiver that declares
    /// parameters.
    /// @see `whileFalse:`.
    public whileFalse = (
      ^[self value] whileFalse.
    )

    /// Evaluates the receiver again and again, without end: only a
    /// non-local return out of it, an exception or the end of the program
    /// ends the loop.
    ///
    /// The compiler inlines a send of this message whose receiver is a
    /// block literal, a `^` in it then the method's own return; this
    /// method serves every other send.
    ///
    /// @answers nothing: the send never answers.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying the block, 'wrong number of block
    /// arguments: block takes …, got 0', for a receiver that declares
    /// parameters.
    /// @see `whileTrue`.
    public repeat = (
      [self value] repeat.
    )

    /// Evaluates the receiver. An exception signalled meanwhile whose
    /// class `exceptionClass handles:` runs `handler`, given the exception.
    ///
    /// ANSI's handler: the marker on this method's code tells `signal`
    /// this activation handles `exceptionClass` with `handler`, while
    /// `handlerActive` is true (docs/design/core-library.md,
    /// "Exceptions"). The body is a tail send that tail-call elimination
    /// must never skip (docs/design/execution.md, "Planned: tail calls").
    ///
    /// @param exceptionClass an exception class, or anything understanding
    /// `handles:`; sent `handles:` with each exception signalled, while
    /// this `on:do:` is disabled.
    /// @param handler a block of no argument or one, or anything
    /// understanding `cull:`; sent `cull:` with the exception.
    /// @answers the receiver's value; or, once `handler` runs, the
    /// handler's value, unless it resumes, retries or passes the exception,
    /// or ends this send with `return:`, whose argument it answers, or
    /// `return`, which answers nil.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying the receiver, 'wrong number of block
    /// arguments: block takes …, got 0', for a receiver that declares
    /// parameters, unless `exceptionClass` handles it, in which case
    /// `handler` runs with it.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying the block, 'wrong number of block
    /// arguments: block takes …, got 1', for a `handler` block of two
    /// parameters or more, when it runs.
    public on: exceptionClass do: handler = (
      |
        handlerActive = true.
      |
      ^self value.
    )

    /// Evaluates the receiver, then `onUnwind`. `onUnwind` runs exactly
    /// once, also when an unwind abandons the receiver: a `^` out of it,
    /// an exception's `return:`, `retry` or `resume:`, or the end of the
    /// run an unhandled exception brings.
    ///
    /// On a normal end the block runs here; on an unwind the unwinder
    /// runs it, having set `complete` first, so it runs exactly once.
    ///
    /// @param onUnwind a block of no argument, or anything understanding
    /// `value`; sent `value`.
    /// @answers the receiver's value, when the receiver completes.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying the receiver, 'wrong number of block
    /// arguments: block takes …, got 0', for a receiver that declares
    /// parameters; `onUnwind` then runs as the unwind abandons this send.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying the block, 'wrong number of block
    /// arguments: block takes …, got 0', for an `onUnwind` block that
    /// declares parameters, when it runs.
    public ensure: onUnwind = (
      |
        complete ::= nil.
        result = self value.
      |
      complete isNil ifTrue: [
        complete:: true.
        onUnwind value.
      ].
      ^result.
    )

    /// Evaluates the receiver; runs `onUnwind` only when an unwind
    /// abandons the receiver.
    ///
    /// @param onUnwind as `ensure:`'s.
    /// @answers the receiver's value, when the receiver completes.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying the receiver, 'wrong number of block
    /// arguments: block takes …, got 0', for a receiver that declares
    /// parameters; `onUnwind` then runs as the unwind abandons this send.
    /// @signals ArgumentError carrying the block, 'wrong number of block
    /// arguments: block takes …, got 0', for an `onUnwind` block that
    /// declares parameters, when an unwind abandons the receiver.
    /// @see `ensure:`.
    public ifCurtailed: onUnwind = (
      |
        complete = nil.
      |
      ^self value.
    )

    /// Sends `value` to `onUnwind`. The unwinder activates it for an
    /// `ensure:` or `ifCurtailed:` argument that is no block, so that the
    /// unwind carries on from this activation's return.
    ///
    /// An ordinary send of `value`, as the normal path's, whatever that
    /// send decides -- a method, an instantiation -- and this
    /// activation's return is where the unwind carries on
    /// (`interpreter::unwind`). A block the unwinder activates
    /// itself.
    ///
    /// @param onUnwind any object; sent `value`.
    /// @answers what `onUnwind` answers to `value`.
    private valueOnUnwind: onUnwind = (
      ^onUnwind value.
    )
  )

  /// Runs a full collection: every object that nothing but weak slots
  /// reaches is reclaimed, and those slots read nil from then on.
  /// `platform kernel garbageCollect` sends it.
  ///
  /// The leaf asks for the collection, and the run loop serves it at its
  /// next safepoint: the return from the method that sent this one,
  /// before that method's sender runs on. The leaf never declines; its
  /// failure block answers the receiver, as the leaf does, rather than
  /// resending to `super`, so that no MessageNotUnderstood could ever
  /// carry the kernel instance.
  ///
  /// @answers the receiver, the kernel instance.
  public garbageCollect = (
    ^vmMirror garbageCollect: self ifFail: [self].
  )
)
